    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d873">

                <pb facs="1149" n="1139" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg1139"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Chase, Augustus: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Smyth</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-05-06T11:00:00+08:00">May 6, 1946—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 6—6 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>752. [To Mukden:] Proposal in your unnumbered April 30, 4 p.m.<anchor n="26"
                        xml:id="d873-f1"/> that Chase proceed Harbin accompanied by Rigg,
                    communications equipment, and such personnel as you deem immediately essential
                    as soon as transportation available is approved.</p>
                <p>Executive Headquarters [at] Peiping has been informed to offer you assistance.
                    You should consult Robertson<anchor n="27" xml:id="d873-f2"/> [at] Peiping
                    before making approach Communist representatives Mukden.</p>
                <p>Sent to Mukden as 7, May 6, 11 a.m., repeated to Dept. as 752; repeated to
                    Peiping for Robertson as 45.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smyth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
